WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.856
These stations practise the school’s medical-device objectives. Begin by identifying the device and patient’s immediate condition. The lecture teaches observation, communication and escalation; it is not a procedure manual.
这些器械站练习学校的医疗器械目标。开始时先识别器械并评估患者即时状况。本课训练观察、沟通和升级处置，不是操作手册。

00:00:14.856 --> 00:00:32.712
Do not remove or reposition a displaced device unless the immediate-life-threat exception explicitly applies and the action is authorized and taught. In this lab, do not insert, flush, reconnect, inflate or test a device without direct instructor instruction.
除非明确符合立即生命威胁的例外，且行动获得授权并接受过训练，否则不要拔除或重置移位器械。在本实验中，未经教官直接指示，不要插入、冲洗、重新连接、充气或测试器械。

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:48.456
The instructor supplies a manikin or photo showing an enteral tube that appears displaced. State what is visible, how the family describes the change and what you cannot confirm. Ask when it was last used and whether feeding or medicine was given afterward.
教官提供一个模型或图片，显示肠内管路似乎发生移位。说明可见情况、家属如何描述变化以及哪些信息无法确认。询问上次使用时间，以及此后是否进行过喂养或给药。

00:00:48.456 --> 00:01:04.992
Assess the patient’s condition and the site without testing or advancing the tube. Report pain, vomiting, leakage, bleeding or worsening perfusion; communicate that the device should not be used until its status is confirmed by the appropriate clinician.
评估患者和入口处情况，但不要测试或推进管路。报告疼痛、呕吐、渗漏、出血或灌注恶化；明确说明在合适的临床人员确认之前不应使用该器械。

00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:21.288
Use the supplied chart or bag demonstration to report measured output and the time interval. Separate a staff estimate from a recorded measurement. Ask about the patient’s usual output, recent intake, baseline cognition and the timing of new symptoms.
使用提供的记录表或尿袋演示，报告实测尿量和时间间隔。区分工作人员估计和实际记录。询问患者平时尿量、近期摄入、认知基线及新症状出现时间。

00:01:21.288 --> 00:01:37.968
A suspected blockage is not an invitation to manipulate the catheter. The PCP’s scope does not automatically include urinary catheterization, and school practice does not grant extra endorsement. Escalate the patient’s condition through current service pathways.
怀疑堵塞不意味着可以操作导尿管。PCP 权限并不自动包括导尿操作，学校练习也不会额外授予执照背书。应依据现行服务流程升级处理患者状况。

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:53.544
In an ostomy station, describe the appliance and visible skin without removing the pouch. Ask what is normal for this person, when the output changed, whether there is pain or leakage and whether food, fluid or medication intake changed.
在造口站，应描述器具和可见皮肤，但不要移除造口袋。询问患者的正常状态、排出物何时改变、是否疼痛或渗漏，以及食物、液体或药物摄入是否变化。

00:01:53.544 --> 00:02:11.184
The goal is to notice possible dehydration, skin injury or acute abdominal change and share the facts with the receiving team. Do not insert a finger, probe the stoma or attempt an appliance procedure unless a specific current protocol and instructor supervision authorize it.
目标是识别可能的脱水、皮肤损伤或急性腹部变化，并向接收团队准确传递信息。除非有具体现行规程和教官监督授权，否则不要把手指伸入、探查造口或尝试操作器具。

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:27.264
The integrated weekend scenario combines a device concern with a second patient who may have a more immediate threat. Before dividing, state the priority and the reason. Assign a named partner to each task and set an exact trigger for a check-back.
综合周末情景将器械问题与另一名可能有更紧迫威胁的患者结合。在分工前先说出优先事项和原因。为每项任务指定队友，并明确复查触发点。

00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:42.720
Do not allow the first patient to go unobserved while the second patient is assessed. Use short status updates, repeat the priority when the situation changes and request additional resources early if one crew cannot safely cover both patients.
评估第二名患者时，不能让第一名患者无人观察。应进行简短状态更新，情况变化时重新说明优先事项；一组人员无法安全照顾两人时，应及早请求增援。

00:02:42.720 --> 00:03:02.616
For a patient with an enteral tube issue, include device type, apparent displacement, last known use, site findings, abdominal symptoms and whether the tube remained untouched. For a catheter issue, include measured output and period, appearance, reported blockage and systemic cues.
肠内管问题交接应包括器械类型、可见移位、最后使用时间、入口处发现、腹部症状，以及是否保持未操作。导尿管问题应报告实测尿量及时间段、外观、疑似堵塞和全身线索。

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:28.320
For school practice, use the assigned SBAR or MIST format. Current BCEHS A zero three instead specifies ATMIST AMBO for care transitions and SBAR for consultation. State suspected sepsis or suspected abdominal injury as a concern, not a proven diagnosis. Give the actual findings, your request and the response, and verify accepted responsibility.
学校练习使用指定的SBAR或MIST格式；现行BCEHS A03则规定责任交接使用ATMIST AMBO，咨询使用SBAR。疑似脓毒症或腹部损伤应作为担忧，而非已证实诊断。报告实际发现、请求与回应，并核实后续责任已被接受。

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:57.264
These are fictional training data, not clinical thresholds. At ten twenty, patient A is awake, oriented and speaking normally, with abdominal pain rated six of ten. The caregiver now clarifies that the tube was last used at nine and moved at ten ten. The external mark changed and the dressing is moist. Internal position and injury remain unconfirmed. Do not use or manipulate the tube.
以下为虚构训练资料，不是临床阈值。10:20，A患者清醒、定向正常且能正常说话，腹痛六分。照护者现澄清：管路上次使用为09:00，10:10发生移动。外部标记改变，敷料潮湿；内部位置和损伤仍未确认，管路保持停用且不操作。

00:03:57.264 --> 00:04:25.344
Patient B has new confusion, rapid breathing, low pressure and fever; the collection record shows thirty millilitres over six hours. Prioritize the immediate breathing and perfusion threats, request appropriate help and use the current pathway. Assign suitable care and check-back triggers for both patients. Neither a catheter infection nor sepsis is proven, and a device repair must not replace whole-patient care.
B患者新发意识混乱、呼吸快、低血压并发热；收集记录为六小时三十毫升。优先处理即时呼吸与灌注威胁，请求适当支援并采用现行路径。同时为两名患者安排合适照护及回报触发点。导尿管感染和脓毒症均未证实，器械维修不能替代整体照护。

00:04:25.344 --> 00:05:06.432
For B, rehearse this SBAR consultation: I need urgent clinical support for a care-home patient with new confusion, rapid breathing and low pressure. Staff report a normally interactive baseline; the collection record shows thirty millilitres in six hours. At ten twenty, respirations are thirty, pulse one eighteen, pressure eighty-six over fifty-two, saturation ninety-two percent on room air and temperature thirty-eight point six. I am concerned about systemic illness including possible sepsis. Please advise the receiving plan and additional resources while we continue indicated support.
为B练习SBAR咨询：一名护理院患者新发意识混乱、呼吸快且血压低，需要紧急临床支援。工作人员说平时可正常互动，收集记录显示六小时三十毫升。10:20呼吸30次、脉搏118次、血压86/52、室内空气血氧92%、体温38.6℃。担忧全身性疾病，包括可能脓毒症。我们继续提供有指征的支持，请就接收计划及增援提出建议。

00:05:06.432 --> 00:05:51.144
For patient A, give this school report using mechanism, illness, signs and treatment: movement reportedly shifted the feeding tube at ten ten; new abdominal pain and nausea, with a moist dressing and changed external mark, but no confirmed internal injury. At ten twenty, respirations twenty, pulse ninety-six, pressure one eighteen over seventy-two, saturation ninety-seven percent on room air and pain six of ten. We assessed the patient, protected the tube from use or manipulation and are arranging appropriate evaluation with the patient. This is a school report example, not a replacement for the current service transfer format.
为A练习学校MIST：据报10:10移动时喂养管移位；新发腹痛、恶心，敷料潮湿且外部标记改变，但内部损伤未确诊。10:20呼吸20次、脉搏96次、血压118/72、室内空气血氧97%、疼痛六分。已评估患者，保护管路、避免使用或操作，并与患者安排适当评估。这是学校报告示例，不替代现行服务交接格式。

00:05:51.144 --> 00:06:25.272
For the documentation branch, the simulator supplies these later events. At ten thirty, patient A has the same measured values and pain score. The patient accepts assessment and conveyance. The tube is not used, and no medicine is administered. Another qualified crew accepts patient B at ten twenty-eight. Patient A departs at ten thirty-one and the receiving clinician accepts this patient at ten forty-five. These are additional fictional facts for this branch, not events you may assume in another case.
在记录分支中，模拟器补充以下事件：10:30，A的实测数值与疼痛评分不变。A接受评估与转运，管路持续停用，未给药。另一组合适机组于10:28接受B；A于10:31出发，接收临床人员于10:45接受A。这些是本分支新增的虚构事实，不能在其他案例中自行假定。

00:06:25.272 --> 00:07:28.608
A concise A-only narrative could read: At ten twenty, a fifty-five-year-old woman at home reports new abdominal pain and nausea. Caregiver reports the feeding tube was last used at nine and shifted at ten ten. Awake, oriented, speaking normally; respirations twenty, pulse ninety-six, pressure one eighteen over seventy-two, room-air saturation ninety-seven percent, pain six of ten. Dressing moist and external mark changed; internal position not confirmed. Tube not used or manipulated; assessment and conveyance accepted, no medicine given. At ten thirty, measurements and pain unchanged. Departed ten thirty-one; receiving clinician accepted at ten forty-five. Add the actual identifiers, required assessment, medicines, allergies and responsible names from the scenario; unavailable facts stay unavailable. Keep B in a separate record.
A的简明独立叙述可写为：10:20，55岁女性在家报告新发腹痛及恶心。照护者称管路最后使用09:00，10:10移位。清醒、定向正常、说话正常；呼吸20次、脉搏96次、血压118/72、室内空气血氧97%、疼痛六分。敷料潮湿、外部标记改变，内部位置未确认。管路保持停用，未操作；患者接受评估与转运，未给药。10:30实测值及疼痛不变，10:31出发，10:45接收临床人员接受。还须根据真实情景补充身份、必需评估、用药、过敏和责任人姓名；缺失事实仍标缺失。B另写一份记录。

00:07:28.608 --> 00:07:45.192
The school plan sets a five-minute completion target for a legal PCR practice. Treat the time limit as a training constraint, not permission to omit required information or a claim about the law. Use only the school rubric and authorized practice environment.
学校计划把五分钟完成合法 PCR 设为练习目标。应把时限视作训练约束，而不是遗漏必需信息的许可或法律时限的声明。只能使用学校评分表和获准的练习环境。

00:07:45.192 --> 00:08:07.992
Build a truthful timeline first. Then record the patient’s baseline, device status, objective findings, authorized actions and response. Include names or roles, consultation and handover. Each patient needs a separate record; never merge two patients into one narrative or invent a value to meet the timer.
先建立真实时间线，再记录患者基线、器械状态、客观发现、获准行动及反应。包括人员姓名或角色、咨询及交接。每位患者都需要独立记录；不要把两位患者合并进一份叙述，也不能为了赶时间捏造数值。

00:08:07.992 --> 00:08:24.264
At the end of the timed drill, compare the PCR with the scenario record and team observations. Correct chronology, source attribution, device details and patient response. Separate “not assessed” from “normal” and estimate from measurement.
计时练习结束后，应将 PCR 与情景记录及团队观察比较。核对时间顺序、信息来源、器械细节和患者反应。区分“未评估”和“正常”，也区分估计值与实测值。

00:08:24.264 --> 00:08:39.672
A legally and clinically useful record reflects what happened rather than what should have happened. If a safety event or medication error occurred, follow the actual service reporting and amendment process instead of silently editing the narrative.
具有法律和临床价值的记录反映实际发生的事情，而不是本应发生的事情。若出现安全事件或用药错误，应遵循真实服务报告和修订流程，而不是悄悄改写记录。

00:08:39.672 --> 00:08:54.600
The instructor will not lead the review. Ask the seven questions in order, using the patient story and observable evidence. If your answer relies on hindsight, state what information was available at the time and what was not.
复盘由学习者主导。按顺序提出七个问题，结合患者情况和可观察证据回答。若答案依赖事后信息，应说明当时掌握了什么、缺少什么。

00:08:54.600 --> 00:09:11.256
The final question should produce one observable action for the next run: for example, state the source and time for each device-output figure, or assign the second patient a reassessment interval. The instructor may then calibrate the target against the rubric.
最后一个问题应为下一轮设定一个可观察行为，例如每个器械输出数值都注明来源和时间，或为第二名患者指定复评间隔。随后由教官按评分表校准目标。

00:09:11.256 --> 00:09:26.520
End each station by summarizing the patient’s concern, relevant device change, main findings, actions, response and next concern. Use neutral language and preserve the person’s dignity during examination and movement.
每个器械站结束时，应总结患者担忧、相关器械变化、主要发现、采取的行动、患者反应和下一项担忧。检查和移动患者时使用中性语言并维护其尊严。

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:44.256
This week practises NG/PEG, urinary-catheter and ostomy scenarios. The purpose is recognition, reasoning, communication and documentation under supervision—not independent device manipulation or competency sign-off from an online lesson.
本周练习 NG/PEG、导尿管和造口情景。目标是在监督下进行识别、推理、沟通和记录，而不是通过在线课程独立操作器械或取得能力认证。
